      "title": "Temporary Museum Membership Associate",
      "description": "Temporary Museum Membership Associate - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Temporary Museum Membership Associate NSU Art Museum Ready to Apply? Temporary Museum Membership Associate 508574 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Museum Services Temporary Closing on: Sep 10 2027 NSU Art Museum Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Open and close lobby membership desk, count till, record money. Staff lobby membership desk on scheduled days during regular museum hours. Greet and assist members and other visitors with membership and ticket inquiries and issues with excellent customer service. Contact a manager to help resolve larger problems. Process membership and ticket purchases and update required information on member ticket form. Answer and return phone calls. Must be able to answer questions regarding programs, exhibitions. Support and work under direction of Donor Relations Associate and Annual Fund Manager in strategies and projects to grow the membership base and revenue; achieve a high retention rate and upgrades among renewing members. Job Category: Non-Exempt Hiring Range: $16.00 per hour Pay Basis: Hourly Subject to Grant Funding? No Essential Job Functions: Open and close lobby membership desk, count till, record money. Staff lobby membership desk on scheduled days during regular museum hours. Greet and assist members and other visitors with membership and ticket inquiries and issues with excellent customer service. Contact a manager to help resolve larger problems. Process membership and ticket purchases and update required information on member ticket form. Answer and return phone calls. Able to answer questions regarding programs. Promote and solicit new, renewed, and upgraded membership among callers, visitors, and in off-site development initiatives. Provide clerical assistance in the development office as needed. Provide check-in and check-out assistance at member events as needed. (Free parking is available.) Support in the management of volunteer-based program to make follow up calls to members on Development/Fundraising activities. Performs other duties as needed and directed by supervisor. Job Requirements: Superb people skills both in person and via phone. Enthusiastic and positive attitude. Dedication to the principles of good customer service. Detail oriented, good judgment and discretion in assisting members. Possess great computer skills. Bilingual is a plus. Box office or concierge experience a plus. Request days off in advance. Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Understand the principles of philanthropy, with particular emphasis on major gifts, grants, sponsorships, and foundations. Strong organizational ability, analytical skills, and attention to detail. Exceptional judgement, professionalism, and discretion in handling confidential and sensitive situations and matters. Flexible work schedule, with availability to work nights, weekends, and holidays, as needed. Ability to multi-task Required Certifications/Licensures: None Required Education: High School Diploma or equivalent Major (if required: Required Experience: A minimum of 1 year of experience in Customer Service Preferred Qualifications: Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? Yes Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert 8b44d526 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Museum Services Museum Services Locations Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States First Name (required) 9ce082d9 Last Name (required) 4a8400df Email (required) 21b75bdb Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at NSU.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and 