    "https://nsucareers.nova.edu/jobs/faculty-rank-tbd-psychiatry-and-program-director-psychiatry-residency-991301-orlando-florida-united-states-clearwater": {
      "title": "Faculty (Rank TBD), Psychiatry and Program Director, Psychiatry Residency",
      "description": "Faculty (Rank TBD), Psychiatry and Program Director, Psychiatry Residency - 991301 - Orlando, Florida, United States - Clearwater, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Faculty (Rank TBD), Psychiatry and Program Director, Psychiatry Residency - 991301 K. Patel College of Osteopathic Med Ready to Apply? Faculty (Rank TBD), Psychiatry and Program Director, Psychiatry Residency - 991301 508620 3400 Gulf to Bay Blvd, Clearwater, Florida, United States, 33759 4850 Millenia Blvd, Orlando, Florida, United States, 32839 Faculty - Health Professions Research, Service, & Sponsored Programs Part Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Dec 31 2026 K. Patel College of Osteopathic Med Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Oversees the ACGME-accredited Psychiatry Residency Program. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with experience Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? Yes Essential Job Functions: 1. Oversees administration and operation of psychiatry residency and residents. 2. Provides resident recruitment and supervision. 3. Maintains a training program aligned with ACGME specific requirements. 4. Ensures all aspects of psychiatry program meet accreditation standards. 5. Provides clinical care to patients. 6. Performs other duties as assigned or required. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Knowledge 1. Comprehensive knowledge of psychiatry principles, diagnosis, treatment modalities, and evidence-based practices. 2. Knowledge of ACGME Institutional and Psychiatry Program Requirements. 3. Knowledge of residency education, curriculum development, competency-based medical education, and assessment methodologies. 4. Knowledge of accreditation, regulatory, and compliance standards governing graduate medical education. 5. Knowledge of healthcare delivery systems, quality improvement, patient safety initiatives, and risk management practices. Skills 1. Strong leadership and organizational skills to direct, manage, and evaluate a psychiatry residency program. 2. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including presentation and public speaking abilities. 3. Skill in curriculum design, implementation, and continuous program improvement. 4. Ability to effectively mentor, coach, and develop residents and faculty members. 5. Strong interpersonal and conflict-resolution skills. 6. Skill in data analysis and interpretation for accreditation reporting, resident performance evaluation, and program assessment. 7. Effective project management and strategic planning skills. 8. Ability to manage budgets, resources, schedules, and operational priorities. 9. Proficiency with educational technologies, electronic health records, and residency management systems. 10. Skill in conducting performance evaluations and providing constructive feedback. Abilities 1. Ability to maintain ACGME accreditation standards and successfully prepare for site visits and reviews. 2. Ability to recruit, retain, and develop high-performing residents and faculty. 3. Ability to collaborate effectively with institutional leadership, faculty, clinical staff, and community partners. 4. Ability to balance clinical, educational, administrative, and scholarly responsibilities. 5. Ability to analyze complex situations and make sound, timely decisions. 6. Ability to promote a culture of professionalism, accountability, and continuous improvement. 7. Ability to assess program outcomes and implement evidence-based changes. 8. Ability to adapt to changing accreditation requirements, healthcare trends, and organizational priorities. Required Certifications/Licensures: 1. Board certification in Psychiatry 2. State of Florida License Required Education: Terminal Degree (DO or MD degree) Major (if required: Osteopathic Medicine or Allopathic Medicine Required Experience: Terminal D.O. or M.D. degree with board certification in Psychiatry Preferred Qualifications: 1. Prior teaching experience in clinical, academic or administrative role. 2. Prior experience as Program Director or Associate Program Director 3. Strong interpersonal skills and written communication skills 4. Leadership or administrative experience Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? Yes Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be no