      "title": "Faculty (Rank TBD)",
      "description": "Faculty (Rank TBD) - Clinical Forensic Psychology - 997392 - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Faculty (Rank TBD) - Clinical Forensic Psychology - 997392 College of Psychology Ready to Apply? Faculty (Rank TBD) - Clinical Forensic Psychology - 997392 508456 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Full Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Jan 8 2027 College of Psychology Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: The faculty member is responsible for teaching, providing clinical supervision, and mentoring student research in the doctoral clinical and school psychology programs. Evidence of scholarly productivity is required. A track record of, or potential to secure, external funding to support research is desirable. Faculty rank is commensurate with experience and credentials. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with experience Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? Essential Job Functions: 1. Teaches courses in clinical and forensic psychology in the doctoral programs in clinical psychology. 2. Maintains an active research program and develop peer-reviewed publications. 3. Mentors doctoral students in research. 4. Creates a climate that is conducive to learning. 5. Supports the mission of the College by demonstrating flexibility in meeting program needs for supervision, and/or meetings. 6. Participates in department-wide activities such as faculty meetings, chairing dissertations and directed study projects, clinical competency examinations, and other service activities as assigned. 7. Contributes expertise in the area of forensic psychology. 8. Serves and contributes to appropriate department, college, university, and national committees. 9. Maintains a professional development plan to assure growth and currency within the academic field. 10. Performs other duties as assigned or required by the Department Chair and/or Dean. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Required Certifications/Licensures: Licensed or license-eligible in the State of Florida. Required Education: Doctoral Degree Major (if required: Clinical, Counseling Psychology or related field Required Experience: 1. University teaching experience. 2. A record of scholarly publications. 3. Clinical/scholarly expertise in forensic psychology Preferred Qualifications: 1. Five (5) years teaching graduate level courses in psychology or related field. 2. Supervision experience. 3. Potential to secure external funding to support a research program. Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? Yes Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Join Our Talent Network First Name (required) c117a46f Last Name (required) ea2cc1cd Email (required) 8e1101c9 Phone Number 38d3b5a7 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) Dominican Republic (+1) Ecuador (+593) Egypt (+20) El Salvador (+503) Equatorial Guinea (+240) Eritrea (+291) Estonia (+372) Eswatini (+268) Ethiopia (+251) Falkland Islands (Islas Malvinas) (+500) Faroe Islands (+298) Fiji (+679) Finland (+358) France (+33) French Guiana (+594) French Polynes