    "https://nsucareers.nova.edu/jobs/adjunct-conflict-analysis-and-resolution-department-fort-lauderdale-davie-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "ADJUNCT-Conflict Analysis and Resolution Department",
      "description": "ADJUNCT-Conflict Analysis and Resolution Department - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode ADJUNCT-Conflict Analysis and Resolution Department Halmos College Of Arts and Sciences Ready to Apply? ADJUNCT-Conflict Analysis and Resolution Department 508406 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Adjunct Faculty Closing on: Jul 31 2027 Halmos College Of Arts and Sciences Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: The Halmos College of Arts and Sciences and Guy Harvey Oceanographic Research Center (HCAS) of Nova Southeastern University (NSU) is seeking adjunct faculty to teach graduate and doctoral-level courses for NSU. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with Experience Pay Basis: Subject to Grant Funding? No Essential Job Functions: 1. Teach assigned courses professionally and in accordance with university, college, and program requirements. 2. Prepare and submit course syllabi by established deadlines. 3. Maintain regular and professional communication with students and the program supervisor. 4. Respond to student and supervisor communications within 48 hours. 5. Provide students with timely and substantive feedback on assignments, assessments, and academic progress. 6. Submit grades, progress reports, attendance information, and other required documentation accurately and by established deadlines. 7. Maintain appropriate course and student records and provide them to the program supervisor when requested. Job Requirements: Demonstrated ability to teach effectively in an online learning environment and to use learning management systems, videoconferencing platforms, email, and other instructional technologies required for course delivery. Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: 1. Demonstrated expertise appropriate for teaching graduate and doctoral-level courses in conflict analysis and resolution. 2. Ability to connect theory, research, and practice in the classroom and to mentor doctoral students. 3. Strong written, oral, interpersonal, organizational, and instructional technology skills. 4. Ability to work effectively with students from diverse academic, cultural, and professional backgrounds. 5. Adjunct faculty may also be asked to serve as members of dissertation committees when their expertise aligns with a student’s research. Required Certifications/Licensures: Required Education: Doctoral Degree Major (if required: Conflict Analysis and Resolution, Peace and Conflict Studies, Peacebuilding, or a closely related field from a regionally accredited institution or its international equivalent. Required Experience: 1. Demonstrated expertise related to the assigned course. 2. Prior graduate teaching and online teaching experience preferred. 3. Practitioner experience preferred for practice courses, ethics, public policy, and practicum courses. 4. Research-methods expertise required for quantitative, qualitative, research design, or dissertation-related courses. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Prior experience teaching graduate or doctoral-level courses. 2. Prior experience teaching in an online or blended-learning environment. 3. Professional practice experience in mediation, negotiation, facilitation, conflict intervention, peacebuilding, public policy, organizational conflict, community conflict, ethics, or another area relevant to the assigned course. 4. Experience mentoring doctoral students or serving on dissertation committees. 5. Evidence of scholarship, applied research, or professional service in conflict analysis and resolution or a related field. Is this a safety sensitive position? Background Screening Required? Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert dbe28acc Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Locations Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Fort Lauderdale