      "title": "Faculty (Rank TBD), Occupational Therapy and Academic Field Coordinator",
      "description": "Faculty (Rank TBD), Occupational Therapy and Academic Field Coordinator - 993530 - Clearwater, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Faculty (Rank TBD), Occupational Therapy and Academic Field Coordinator - 993530 K. Patel College of Osteopathic Med Ready to Apply? Faculty (Rank TBD), Occupational Therapy and Academic Field Coordinator - 993530 508281 3400 Gulf to Bay Blvd, Clearwater, Florida, United States, 33759 Faculty - Health Professions Full Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Jan 31 2027 K. Patel College of Osteopathic Med Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Performs all administrative tasks associated directly with clinical activities, student discipline, clinical policy, and student rotation assignments and is responsible for the overall coordination and organization of the Fieldwork operations. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with experience Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? No Essential Job Functions: 1. Ensures continued compliance with university and program policies & procedures, as well as ACOTE Standards for Fieldwork (FW). 2. Places students to FW sites in accordance to curricular requirements. 3. Responds to students' queries in matters pertaining to fieldwork. 4. Maintains fieldwork site files in accordance with department policies and accreditation requirements. 5. Ensures clinical educators and FW site meet established ACOTE Standards. 6. Reviews and updates FW policies and procedures. 7. Oversees student orientation to FW assignments and FW policies and procedures. 8. Researches, implements, and maintains a computer database that will track FW site/FW educator effectiveness, student progress, student placement, etc. 9. Monitors student progress while they are in level-1 and level-2 FW. 10. Coordinates new site development and works with NSU legal counsel to obtain and maintain appropriate affiliation agreements. 11. Manages individual FW issues as they occur. 12. Identifies students at risk of failing FW, and follows established procedures. 13. Supervises FW support staff to ensure compliance with ACOTE Standards and department policies and procedures. 14. Teaches FW related courses, including content for mandatory compliance training, to include CPR, licensures requirements, etc. 15. Ensures students have met all requirements for FW, including medical immunizations, background checks, and other requirements as they develop. 16. Ensures clear and timely communication between students on FW, FW educator, and appropriate course instructors. 17. Ensures that FW sites and FW educators are in congruence with program's curricular design and ACOTE Standards, including continuing education of FW educators. 18. Provides and maintains a reliable schedule of office hours for student advising, tutoring, remediation and consultation. 19. Teaches assigned courses with a focus on occupation- and evidence-based practice and teaching and evaluation strategies appropriate to the students and setting. 20. Collaborates with fellow faculty members within the department, college, and division to develop and participate in courses, research projects, university & community service, and scholarly activities. 21. Engages in curriculum development related to current and new courses. 22. Engages in scholarly activities within and outside of the department. 23. Supervises and direct activities of clinical faculty. 24. Performs other duties as assigned or required. Job Requirements: Appointment to the rank of professor requires a record of distinguished scholarship and outstanding teaching ability, evidenced by recognized professional productivity in the field(s) of specialization. Appointment to the rank of associate professor normally requires a record of substantial success in teaching, scholarship, and service. Appointment to the rank of assistant professor requires completion of professional training, which in most disciplines will be a terminal degree (usually the earned doctorate),and the clear promise of a successful career in teaching, scholarship, and service. Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: 1. Ability to read, analyze, and interpret common scientific and technical journals. 2. Ability to effectively present information to students, public groups, or professional organizations in the English language. 3. Ability to work with appropriate mathematical concepts specific to the particular discipline. 4. Ability to apply concepts to practical situations. 5. Ability to apply principles of logical or scientific thinking to a wide range of intellectual and practical problems. 6. Ability to deal with nonverbal symbolism (formulas, scientific equations, graphs, etc.). Required Certifications/Licensures: 1. Initial National Board Certification in Occupational Therapy (NBCOT) 2. State of Florida licensure required as of date of hire. Required Education: Doctoral Degree Major (if required: Occupational Therapy or related area of specialization. Required Experience: 1. Five (5) years of relevant experience, including at least two (2) years of clinical experience, along with demonstrated evidence of scholarship. 2. Must be a graduate of an accredited Occupational Therapy program. Preferred Qualifications: Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? No Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert 4142ec79 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty - Health Professions Faculty - Health Professions Locations Clearwater, Florida, United States Clearwater, Florida, United States First Name (required) 10b402f3 Last Name (required) eeecca11 Email (required) 1fa4f2dd Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at NSU.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Priva