    "https://nsucareers.nova.edu/jobs/adjunct-faculty-dr-pallavi-patel-school-of-health-sciences-fort-lauderdale-davie-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty - Dr. Pallavi Patel School of Health Sciences - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty - Dr. Pallavi Patel School of Health Sciences K.Patel Coll of Allopathic Medicine Ready to Apply? Adjunct Faculty - Dr. Pallavi Patel School of Health Sciences 508115 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Health Professions Adjunct Faculty Closing on: May 7 2029 K.Patel Coll of Allopathic Medicine Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the Dr. Pallavi Patel School of Health Sciences. Job Category: Hiring Range: Pay Basis: Subject to Grant Funding? Essential Job Functions: 1. Prepare and deliver instruction to students in the Dr. Pallavi Patel School of Health Sciences. 2. Facilitate activities in the classroom and/or laboratory. 3. Act as a liaison between the students and the Faculty Course Coordinator, Program Director, and/or Chair. 4. Provide and facilitate examinations. May include assigning grades consistent with course requirements. 5. Teach or facilitate classes based on varied schedules to accommodate diverse student needs and to meet the expectations of the College. 6. Follow the course curriculum as assigned. 7. Prepare assignments as necessary. 8. Evaluate student performance and learning as assigned. 9. Maintain an active classroom environment conducive to student learning and success. 10. Adjuncts working in the laboratories may also engage in patient or healthcare professional role play, small group discussions, and skill facilitation. 11. Required to complete NSU mandatory trainings. For example, HIPAA compliance, technology training, Canvas training, etc. 12. Performs other related duties as assigned by either the Program Director, Chair, or Faculty Course Coordinator. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Required Certifications/Licensures: Required Education: Master's Degree Major (if required: Required Experience: Preferred Qualifications: Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? No Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert ff51c020 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the