    "https://nsucareers.nova.edu/jobs/medical-education-specialist-and-faculty-rank-tbd-medical-education-991616-clearwater-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Medical Education Specialist and Faculty (Rank TBD), Medical Education",
      "description": "Medical Education Specialist and Faculty (Rank TBD), Medical Education - 991616 - Clearwater, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Medical Education Specialist and Faculty (Rank TBD), Medical Education - 991616 K. Patel College of Osteopathic Med Ready to Apply? Medical Education Specialist and Faculty (Rank TBD), Medical Education - 991616 508388 3400 Gulf to Bay Blvd, Clearwater, Florida, United States, 33759 Faculty - Health Professions Full Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Jan 4 2027 K. Patel College of Osteopathic Med Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Promotes and advances the field of medical education at the COM through student advising and support, faculty development and curricular development. This position must be current on teaching strategies, technologies, and research in medical education. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with experience Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? No Essential Job Functions: 1. Provides guidance to students on various study skills and strategies for learning. 2. Provides curricular support to all degree programs at the COM. 3. Engages and supports the COM in curriculum and program development. 4. Conducts assessment of curriculum, student achievement and learning technologies on regular basis and presents to COM administrators and faculty. 5. Researches current trends and new technologies in health care education to advise and counsel faculty within the COM for purposes of curricular design, modification and implementation. 6. Presents ideas clearly. 7. Performs other duties as assigned or required. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: 1. Must be able to adapt and be willing to teach courses and/or perform special duties as assigned. 2. Participate in state and/or local community service that is recognized from a career development aspect. 3. Ability to read, analyze and interpret common scientific and technical journals. Required Certifications/Licensures: Required Education: Masters Degree Major (if required: Required Experience: 1. Five (5) years of related experience and/or training including research or equivalent combination of education and experience. 2. Excellence in teaching, including on line teaching. 3. Demonstrated experience in curricular and program design, development, and implementation. 4. Experience in curricular planning, faculty development, instructional design and evaluation. 5. Experience in medical education, research and grant writing. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Terminal Degree in Education or related field or a clinical doctorate degree from an accredited institution with demonstrated experience in the health professions. 2. Experience in a medical school or other health professional setting. Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? No Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert 99dad41b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty - Health Professions Faculty - Health Professions Locations Clearwater, Florida, United States Clearwater, Florida, United States First Name (required) 2f4741bc Last Name (required) 23a77bca Email (required) cf0394ed Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at NSU.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy . Thank you Join Our Talent Network First Name (required) 5cbadd9d Last Name (required) 080c73e4 Email (required) dd8d016f Phone Number de6f53d3 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Baha