      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling College of Psychology Ready to Apply? Adjunct Faculty, Clinical Mental Health Counseling 508358 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Adjunct Faculty Closing on: Jan 8 2027 College of Psychology Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Nova Southeastern University's College of Psychology is seeking Adjunct Faculty members for the Clinical Mental Health Counseling master's degree programs. The programs are offered at NSU's main campus in Fort Lauderdale, at NSU campuses in Orlando, Tampa, Miami, and also online. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Pay Basis: Subject to Grant Funding? Essential Job Functions: 1. Professional identity as a counselor educator. 2. Commitment to the professional field of counselor education as evidenced by education, teaching counseling experience, research, and professional affiliations, such as AMHCA, ACES, and ACA. 3. Experience in teaching graduate-level courses. 4. Commitment to multicultural counseling competencies. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Required Certifications/Licensures: Licensed or License Eligible Required Education: Doctoral Degree in Counselor Education (doctoral degree must be earned and conferred by date of hire) Major (if required: Required Experience: 1. Holds terminal doctoral degree from a CACREP-accredited program or related profession and documented experience in the field of clinical mental health counseling. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Licensed or License-eligible as a Professional Counselor or Licensed Mental Health Counselor. 2. Hold Certification or is certification-eligible with NBCC. 3. Active professional involvement with NBCC and ACA. Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? No Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert 72aaa4db Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list o