      "description": "Faculty (Rank TBD) - Psychology (9M) - 993565 - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Faculty (Rank TBD) - Psychology (9M) - 993565 College of Psychology Ready to Apply? Faculty (Rank TBD) - Psychology (9M) - 993565 508183 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Full Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Nov 20 2026 College of Psychology Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Provides high quality instruction in field of expertise to ensure students meet course outcomes. Collaborates with college staff and colleagues to improve students' learning experience, as well asconducting research or scholarship to advance knowledge and mentoring students. Faculty rank is commensurate with experience and credentials. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? Essential Job Functions: 1. Maintains an active research program and develop a strong record of peer-reviewed publications and grant submissions. Area of scholarly expertise is open. 2. Teaches core courses in the psychology programs. The teaching load is contingent on research productivity. 3. Mentors students in research. 4. Creates an environment that is conducive to learning. 5. Serves and contributes to appropriate department, college, and university committees. 6. Maintains a professional development plan to assure growth and currency within the academic field. 7. Performs other duties as assigned or required by the Department Chair and/or the Dean. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Required Certifications/Licensures: Required Education: Doctoral Degree Major (if required: Psychology Required Experience: 1. Record of external funding to support a research program (or evidence of potential to secure external funding). 2. A record of scholarly publications. 3. College and/or university level teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications: The preferred area of scholarly expertise is Clinical/ Health Psychology. Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? No Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert 36945747 Finalize your job aler