      "title": "Faculty (Rank TBD), Counseling (9M)",
      "description": "Faculty (Rank TBD), Counseling (9M) - 992273 - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Faculty (Rank TBD), Counseling (9M) - 992273 College of Psychology Ready to Apply? Faculty (Rank TBD), Counseling (9M) - 992273 508118 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Full Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Nov 20 2026 College of Psychology Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Provides the highest quality education to students in the counselor education programs, including but not limited to teaching, supervision, mentoring, and advising. Engages in scholarly work, including research. Contributes to both the community and the university through service activities. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with experience Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? No Essential Job Functions: 1. Teaches graduate classes in the Clinical Mental Health Counseling program. 2. Supervises students in clinical mental health counseling practicum and internship field placements. 3. Engages in research and scholarship, including generating publications, professional presentations, and grant writing. 4. Provides service to the community and the counseling profession by participating in local, state, an national associations' events, conferences, and committee/board work. 5. Fulfills service responsibilities to the department, college, and university. 6. Provides advisement and mentoring to students in the counseling programs. 7. Utilizes technology in teaching and supervision. 8. Participates in preparation for accreditation (e.g., CACREP) reviews and university-level program reviews. 9. Works in collaboration with other colleagues in the Department of Counseling and in the College of Psychology and community partners. 10. Performs other duties as assigned or required. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Familiarity with classroom management software (e.g., Canvas, Watermark, Zoom). Required Certifications/Licensures: Licensed or License-eligible as a Licensed Mental Health Counselor in the state of Florida. Required Education: Doctoral Degree Major (if required: Required Experience: 1. Doctoral degree in Counselor Education (or were full time faculty in a Counselor Education program prior to July 1, 2013) or ABD. 2. Doctoral degree must be earned and conferred by date of hire. 3. Teaching and related experience; teaching graduate-level coursework in Counselor Education. 4. Provision of Clinical Supervision experience. 5. Clinical experience as a professional counselor. 6. Research experience and/or a record of scholarly publications. 7. Leadership and engagement in relevant professional counseling organization. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Certification or eligible for certification with NBCC. 2. Knowledge of accreditation processes (e.g., CACREP, CAEP). 3. Effective leadership. Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? Yes Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert 7e767ff7 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Locations Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States First Name (required) 894e85ed Last Name (required) 9a78640b Email (required) c0cc1236 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at NSU.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy . Thank you Join Our Talent Network First Name (required) 9cbeb49a Last Name (required) 70d04d28 Email (required) a24371a0 Phone Number e1036db2 244 re