      "title": "Faculty (Rank TBD)",
      "description": "Faculty (Rank TBD) - Objective & Projective Personality Assessment - 997516 - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Faculty (Rank TBD) - Objective & Projective Personality Assessment - 997516 College of Psychology Ready to Apply? Faculty (Rank TBD) - Objective & Projective Personality Assessment - 997516 507961 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Full Time with Full Benefits Closing on: Dec 18 2026 College of Psychology Add to favorites View favorites We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. Primary Purpose: Integrates teaching, research, and clinical services to provide quality education for students. Job Category: Exempt Hiring Range: Commensurate with Experience Pay Basis: Annually Subject to Grant Funding? Essential Job Functions: 1.Teaches core clinical psychology courses in the areas of objective and projective personality assessment. The teaching load is contingent on research productivity. 2. Maintains an active research program, including developing peer-reviewed publications in assessment and related areas. 3. Mentors doctoral students in research. 4. Creates a climate conducive to learning. 5. Participates in department wide activities such as faculty meetings, clinical competency examinations, chairing dissertations/directed studies, etc. as assigned. 6. Contributes to appropriate NSU and College committees, and professional associations. 7. Maintains a professional development plan to assure growth and currency within the academic field. 8. Performs other duties as assigned or required by the Department Chair and/or Dean. Job Requirements: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: 1. Ability to teach assessment courses, especially in the areas of objective personality assessment and projective personality assessment. Required Certifications/Licensures: Licensed or license eligible in the State of Florida. Required Education: Doctoral Degree Major (if required: Clinical, Counseling, or School Psychology or related field Required Experience: 1. Record of external funding to support a research program (or evidence of potential to secure external funding). 2. A record of scholarly publications with a focus on assessment. 3. College and/or university level teaching experience or related training experience in clinical assessment. Preferred Qualifications: 1. Experience training assessment especially in the area of personality assessment. 2. Ability to teach courses in cognitive assessment is a plus but not required. Is this a safety sensitive position? No Background Screening Required? Yes Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. NSU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert b218842b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Faculty - Arts, Humanities, Social Sciences, Psychology, Education Locations Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States First Name (required) 6668debd Last Name (required) ed308d4d Email (required) 19cfb809 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at NSU.  Message & data rates may apply. Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). By submitting your information, you acknowledge that you have read and agree to our Privacy Policy . Thank you Join Our Talent Network First Name (required) b3485f62 Last Name (required) 8d80b1e3 Email (required) b848f2ed Phone Number a0e436fa 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda 