      "title": "Adjunct-HPD Coll of Optometry",
      "description": "Adjunct-HPD Coll of Optometry - Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States Home Search Jobs All Jobs Staff Jobs Faculty Jobs Temporary Jobs Featured Jobs Benefits NSU Culture NSU at a Glance Faculty and Staff News NSU in the News NSU Research NSU Mako Magazine Winter 2025 My Profile Kiosk mode Adjunct-HPD Coll of Optometry College of Optometry Ready to Apply? Adjunct-HPD Coll of Optometry 503825 3300 S University Drive, Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida, United States, 33328 Faculty - Health Professions Adjunct Faculty Closing on: Mar 13 2027 College of Optometry Add to favorites View favorites About Us: We are excited that you are considering joining Nova Southeastern University! Nova Southeastern University (NSU) was founded in 1964, and is a not-for-profit, independent university with a reputation for academic excellence and innovation. Nova Southeastern University offers competitive salaries, a comprehensive benefits package including tuition waiver, retirement plan, excellent medical and dental plans and much more. NSU cares about the health and welfare of its students, faculty, staff, and campus visitors and is a tobacco-free university. We appreciate your support in making NSU the preeminent place to live, work, study and grow. Thank you for your interest in a career with Nova Southeastern University. NSU considers applicants for all positions without regard to race, color, religion, creed, gender, national origin, age, disability, marital or veteran status or any other legally protected status. Job Title: Adjunct-HPD Coll of Optometry Location: Fort Lauderdale-Davie, Florida Work Type: Adjunct Faculty Job Category: Hiring Range: Pay Basis: Subject to Grant Funding?: No Essential Job Functions: 1. Prepares and delivers instruction to OPT. students and/or graduate students. 2. Facilitate activities in the classroom or laboratory. 3. Act as a liaison between the students and the faculty course coordinator. 4. Provide and facilitate examinations. May include assigning grades consistent with course requirements. 5. Teaches or facilitates classes based on varied schedules to accommodate diverse student needs and to meet the expectations of the College as assigned by the designated faculty course coordinator. 6. Follows the course curriculum as assigned. 7. Prepares assignments. 8. Evaluates student performance and learning. 9. Maintains an active classroom environment conducive to student learning and success. 10. Adjuncts working in the laboratories may also engage in patient or healthcare professional role play, small group discussions, and skill facilitation. 11. Required to complete NSU mandatory training. For example, HIPAA compliance, technology training, Canvas training, etc. 12. Performs other related duties as assigned by either the Chair, Assistant Dean, or faculty course coordinator. Marginal Job Functions: Required Knowledge, Skills, & Abilities: Job Requirements: Required Certifications/Licensures: Required Education: Doctoral Degree in related discipline Major (if required): Required Experience: Preferred Qualifications: Is this a safety sensitive position? Background Screening Required? Pre-Employment Conditions: Sensitivity Disclaimer: Nova Southeastern University is in full compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) and does not discriminate with regard to applicants or employees with disabilities, and will make reasonable accommodation when necessary. People Also Viewed TEMPORARY- Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Teacher - (Gr K-5) - 997488 Fort Lauderdale-Davie US-DAVIE LOWER TEMPORARY Administrative Coordinator I Fort Lauderdale-Davie HPD-OSTEOPATHIC MEDICINE-DAVIE Want to be notified when we post new jobs?  Sign up here! Job Alert a08deb7f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of opt